{"job": "N01-baseline", "calls": 2, "questions_counted": 2, "closed": false, "failure": null, "response": {"question": null, "owner_view": "Here is a provisional plan based on what you've told me. You decide whether the evening goes ahead, and you may change the notice a few hours before it starts. You didn't know the answers to my other questions, and I'm treating those as unknown, not as "no". I'm not asking them again.

My advice is to not build custom software yet. Use one simple notice that you can edit yourself from your phone, ideally in a place your members already look. That could be a pinned post in an existing group, a line on an existing club website, or a very basic one-page site if you have nothing. The notice should show the event date, a clear status (ON, OFF or NOT DECIDED YET), and when you last updated it. It should also say when the next decision will be made. Since you may change the decision a few hours beforehand, people need to know to check again on the day.

